# Planning and execution

## Planning

- Small tasks should not produce large plans.
- Large tasks deserve a short, practical plan — in reasoning, not in repository files.
- Do not create temporary Markdown files for planning.
- Avoid expanding scope. Finish one area before moving to another.

## Validation

- Validate important behavior when checks exist.
- Prefer project-native commands (`make`, test runners, linters).
- If a check cannot run, say so. Do not imply success.

## Completion report

At task completion, report only:

- what changed
- what was verified
- what was not verified
- remaining limitations

Keep the report short. Do not repeat planning steps or full implementation details.
